            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'As-Nas is a historical Persian vying game played with a small five-suit pack, using poker-like betting and ranked combinations before modern poker standardized.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'As-Nas was played in Persia with dedicated illustrated cards and is often discussed as part of the broader family of early vying games that predate or parallel poker.',
              },
            ],
          },
